From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Collin Rose <collinr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: fall back to legacy MBSS when interface_create
 is unsupported

Firmware that predates the interface_create iovar, including BCM43602
7.35.177.56, makes the version query in
brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if() fail. The function then returns
-EOPNOTSUPP and never tries bsscfg:ssid. A second AP BSS fails, and
hostapd disables the whole radio, including the primary AP.

Fall through to the legacy MBSS path when the version query fails.
Firmware that answers the query is unchanged.

The same change was first published for a Netgear R8000 on this
firmware, as patches/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch in
88plug/netgear-r8000-plus (GPL-2.0). It is re-ported here onto
backports 7.2. The same early return is still in current mainline
Linux.

Upstream-Status: Submitted to linux-wireless
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/CA+d3OrdhgXy8Dhfi_V=9sEqU=FK4tDzt4HVgOz9Uqw7OTP+8Jg@mail.gmail.com/

Drop this patch once a backports release carries the upstream fix.

https://github.com/88plug/netgear-r8000-plus/blob/netgear-r8000-plus/patches/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch

Tested on a SmartRG SR400ac (bcm53xx, smartrg_sr400ac) with two
BCM43602/1 PCIe radios and brcmfmac43602-pcie firmware 7.35.177.56.
The running image was OpenWrt 25.12.6, mac80211 from backports
6.18.55, on kernel 6.12.112. Without the patch, interface_create v1,
v2, and the version query all return -52, and the driver returns
-EOPNOTSUPP without calling bsscfg:ssid. With the patch, the driver
logs the unsupported version and then creates the second AP. A
primary AP and a second AP stayed up together on 2.4 GHz HT20 and on
5 GHz 80 MHz. The same result held after the patch was built into an
image and the second AP was enabled. A second SR400ac on the same
image and firmware reproduced the unpatched failure. The patched
module was not loaded on that second unit.

The patched site is unchanged between backports 6.18.55 and backports
7.2, which this branch packages. The hunk applies to both.

Signed-off-by: Collin Rose <collinr@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -758,8 +758,9 @@ static int brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if(struct brcmf_if *ifp)
 	err = brcmf_fil_bsscfg_int_query(ifp, "interface_create",
 					 &iface_create_ver);
 	if (err) {
 		brcmf_err("fail to get supported version, err=%d\n", err);
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		/* Old firmware: use the legacy bsscfg:ssid path below. */
+		iface_create_ver = 0;
 	}
 
 	switch (iface_create_ver) {
